<Base
  title="English practitioner map | Andorra residency"
  description="Official Andorran permit codes and 2026 figures, with one English advisor’s A/B/C/D map set beside them. Govern.ad and the BOPA remain the text."
  path="/practitioner-map"
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <h1>An English map, beside the official codes</h1>
    <p>
      Jane Whittaker, an English practitioner, publishes
      <a
        href="https://www.livinginandorra.com/index.html"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">livinginandorra.com</a
      >
      (index dated 19 August 2026). She is listed in the
      <a href="/directory/jane-whittaker">directory</a>.
      After this paragraph, the figures and letter codes are official.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="prose">
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        Her private A/B/C/D is a map, said once: A is official D.1 without
        work; B is D.1.2; C is D.1.3; D is official J.1. Official A.1 is
        employed residence and work. Official B.1 is
        <a href="/family-reunification">family reunification</a>.
        She does not take digital-nomad or entrepreneur files. Govern.ad
        still publishes
        <a href="/digital-nomad">D.3</a>
        and
        <a href="/entrepreneur-residence">D.4</a>.
        The full official list is on
        <a href="/become-a-resident">become a resident</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Compte Propi / J.1</h2>
    <p>
      Govern.ad still shows a live
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball/residencia-i-treball-per-compte-propi-autoritzacio-inicial"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">J.1 page</a
      >,
      a
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia-i-treball/reserva-autoritzacio-de-residencia-i-treball-per-compte-propi"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">J reservation</a
      >,
      and a
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/w/aprovada-una-nova-quota-d-autoritzacions-d-immigracio-de-residencia-i-treball-per-compte-propi-i-de-treball-sense-residencia"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">news note</a
      >
      on Decret 75/2026: a general self-employed quota of 200 (150
      foreign-investment, 50 liberal). Confirm whether a place is actually
      being issued. Longer note:
      <a href="/self-employed-residence">J.1</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Official renewal papers ask for documents proving the company’s
      commercial activity in the period being renewed. They do not set a
      turnover floor.
    </p>

    <h2>Passive investment: Law 2/2026</h2>
    <p>
      Article 96 of
      <a
        href="https://bopadocuments.blob.core.windows.net/bopa-documents/038015/pdf/CGL_2026_02_12_10_11_12.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Law 2/2026 in the BOPA</a
      >
      (in force 13 February 2026) requires at least 1,000,000 euros in
      named Andorran assets for residence without lucrative activity; more
      than 800,000 euros per immovable unit if property is used; and a
      400,000-euro Housing Fund route “in accordance with the applicable
      regulations”. Treat that last figure as a legal possibility, not a
      counter you can walk up to. The AFA income is 50,000 euros for the
      principal plus 12,000 euros per dependant, definitive unless the
      initial authorisation is refused.
    </p>
    <p>
      Card-issue amounts of 3,000 euros / 1,000 euros and a 500-euro
      residence-without-work renewal sit on the
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/altres-tramits/tarifes"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">official tariffs page</a
      >. The 6% / 10% foreign-investment property tax is on a
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/w/s-actualitza-el-reglament-de-l-impost-sobre-la-inversio-estrangera-immobiliaria-d-acord-amb-la-nova-llei-de-continuitat-i-consolidacio-de-les-mesures-per-al-creixement-sostenible"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Govern news note of 26 February 2026</a
      >
      (Decret 58/2026). Ninety days versus 183 days is
      <a href="/tax-residence">immigration versus tax residence</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Passive renewals</h2>
    <p>
      The live
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/tematiques/immigracio/residencia/residencia-sense-treball-autoritzacio-de-renovacio"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">D.2 page</a
      >
      says the 300% + 100% income formula is evidenced, among other
      things, by a pension certificate, a tax return from the last
      country of residence, and bank certifications. The official list is
      enunciative. Read D.2 with counsel.
    </p>

    <h2>Selling property</h2>
    <p>
      The official taxes are the
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/l/4194252"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">impost sobre les plusvàlues</a
      >
      (Law 21/2006, consolidated) and, where it applies, IRPF on capital
      gains. The Government’s IRPF guide describes an exemption for the
      habitual-and-permanent home when the seller is Andorran or can show
      five years’ legal, permanent and continuous residence, and
      reinvests in another habitual home here. Instruct tax counsel
      before a sale.
    </p>

    <h2>EES and the border-management agreement</h2>
    <p>
      A
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/w/condicions-de-circulacio-amb-el-nou-sistema-europeu-entry-exit-ees-"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Govern.ad note of 2 April 2026</a
      >
      states that the European Entry/Exit System, rolled out from October
      2025, is fully operational from <strong>10 April 2026</strong>.
      Andorran nationals are exempt from EES registration under
      Regulation (EU) 2017/2226; so are EU / Schengen nationals and legal
      residents of a member state. The Andorra–EU border-management
      agreement has been initialled (rubricat) but is still pending
      signature, ratification and application:
      <a
        href="https://www.govern.ad/ca/w/andorra-i-la-unio-europea-rubriquen-l-acord-de-gestio-de-fronteres"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Govern news</a
      >
      and
      <a
        href="https://www.andorraue.ad/ca/acords-amb-la-ue/acord-de-gestio-de-fronteres/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">AndorraUE</a
      >.
    </p>
    <p>
      Until that agreement enters into force, the same official note
      tells third-country nationals who hold an Andorran residence permit
      and who wish to travel to Schengen states other than Spain and
      France to check the destination or transit requirements in good
      time. When the agreement applies, Govern.ad says those residents,
      after a security assessment, should be able to make short Schengen
      stays without a visa, ETIAS or EES registration. That is a future
      official promise, not a present practice.
    </p>

    <h2>Driving licences</h2>
    <p>
      The official
      <a
        href="https://www.e-tramits.ad/tramits/renovacio-del-permis-de-conduir/p/GV000303"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">e-tramits renewal</a
      >
      and first-issue pages say the photograph and signature are taken at
      Government premises, by appointment.
    </p>

